 4153 A:149b                                    ; "SYNCHK" LOOKS AT THE CURRENT CHARACTER TO MAKE SURE IT
 4154 A:149b                                    ; IS THE SPECIFIC THING LOADED INTO ACCA JUST BEFORE THE CALL TO
 4155 A:149b                                    ; "SYNCHK". IF NOT, IT CALLS THE "SYNTAX ERROR" ROUTINE.
 4156 A:149b                                    ; OTHERWISE IT GOBBLES THE NEXT CHAR AND RETURNS,
 4157 A:149b                                    ;
 4158 A:149b                                    ; [A]=NEW CHAR AND TXTPTR IS ADVANCED BY "CHRGET".
 4159 A:149b                                    ;
 4160 A:149b                           SYNCHR    
